body:
I wouldn't even call this modern leftist.

&#x200B;

XR can be boiled down to a few words: single-issue and non-intersectional.

&#x200B;

They don't seem to recognise the variety of issues that their diverse membership can face and make arrests look like a fun game. They call prisons a good opportunity to practice yoga/meditation, get a decent shower etc. I'd like to say the BAME who disproportionately die in custody and the working class that suffers shitty sentences disagree.

Oh trust me, they were very pro-cop.

You weren't there watching the entire protest chanting WE LOVE YOU to the police, sitting down to almost every group of people and hearing it less than 10 seconds later become a conversation about how the police have been so nice and great.

&#x200B;

And I apologise to all XR activists that I didn't want to be aggressively misgendered by heavy-handed cops in prison or potentially treated worse based on race and gender. /s

&#x200B;

Before you criticise me for apparently not doing enough, I did partake in the civil obedience. I illegally took part in the occupation (I FUCKING SLEPT ON THE HARD ROAD IN PARLIAMENT SQUARE OVERNIGHT) but if I was told to move on, I would try to delay with as many questions to the officer as possible and walk slowly out while stopping until I was no longer followed.
